sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: How ingest_document and match_node use the TTT service
    accDescr: The SDK uploads a file and gets a job id back at once. It polls the job every second until the state is terminal. On COMPLETED it returns the job status with the graph id; on FAILED it raises JobFailedError. The app then queries one or more graph ids.
    autonumber
    participant App as Your app
    participant SDK as TalkingDBClient
    participant TTT as TTT service
    App->>SDK: ingest_document("report.pdf")
    SDK->>TTT: POST /v1/documents (multipart)
    TTT-->>SDK: 202 job_id, state QUEUED
    loop every poll_interval (1 s)
        SDK->>TTT: GET /v1/jobs/{job_id}
        TTT-->>SDK: state, stage, percent
    end
    alt COMPLETED
        SDK-->>App: JobStatus with result_graph_id
    else FAILED
        SDK-->>App: raise JobFailedError(error_code, message)
    end
    App->>SDK: match_node([graph_id], "question")
    SDK->>TTT: POST /v1/queries
    TTT-->>SDK: elements
    SDK-->>App: list of elements
